# 4. Shared Spaces #

# The canister keeps Hazel's key-value state in named SPACES. Hazel's #
# own space is hazel; any other name is another space, made on first #
# write. A page chooses one, and which of its keys go there, with two #
# settings, window.hazelSpace and window.hazelSpaceKeys, or the URL: #

#   ?space=demo&spaceKeys=scratch: #

# keeps that page's scratch slides in the space demo, on the canister, #
# and everything else in the browser as before. Two browsers that open #
# the same URL edit the same scratch slides. #

# Routes, for a page or a tool: #
#   POST /s/<space>/kv          writes, a batch at a time #
#   GET  /s/<space>/kv          every key, for loading #
#   GET  /spaces                every space and its key count #

# The next step is a deck of its own, Shared Spaces, whose slides #
# live in one space: anyone can add a slide, and everyone sees #
# everyone else's. For the demo, writes are open to anyone. #
()
